{
  "sn7.18:0.1": "Linked Discourses 7.18 ",
  "sn7.18:0.2": "2. Lay Followers ",
  "sn7.18:0.3": "Collecting Firewood ",
  "sn7.18:1.1": "At one time the Buddha was staying in the land of the Kosalans in a certain forest grove. ",
  "sn7.18:1.2": "Then several students, pupils of one of the Bhāradvāja brahmins, approached a forest grove while collecting firewood. They saw the Buddha sitting down cross-legged at the root of a certain sal tree, his body set straight, and mindfulness brought to the present. Seeing this, they went up to Bhāradvāja and said to him, ",
  "sn7.18:1.3": "“Please sir, you should know this. ",
  "sn7.18:1.4": "In such-and-such forest grove the ascetic Gotama is sitting down cross-legged, his body set straight, and mindfulness brought to the present.” ",
  "sn7.18:1.5": "Then Bhāradvāja together with those young students went to that forest grove ",
  "sn7.18:1.6": "where he saw the Buddha sitting down cross-legged, his body set straight, and mindfulness brought to the present. ",
  "sn7.18:1.7": "He went up to the Buddha and addressed him in verse: ",
  "sn7.18:2.1": "“Deep in the jungle so full of terrors, ",
  "sn7.18:2.2": "you’ve plunged into the empty, desolate wilderness. ",
  "sn7.18:2.3": "Still, steady, and graceful: ",
  "sn7.18:2.4": "how beautifully you meditate, mendicant! ",
  "sn7.18:3.1": "Where there is no song or music, ",
  "sn7.18:3.2": "a lonely sage resorts to the wilderness. ",
  "sn7.18:3.3": "This strikes me as an amazing thing, ",
  "sn7.18:3.4": 